## Naming Convention

All assets follow a unified **kebab-case** pattern:

```
{brand}-{category}-{variant}-{theme}[-{size}][-v{N}].{ext}
```

**Segments:**

|Segment              |Values                                                                                      |
|---------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|`{brand}`            |`aioverse`, `aiotize`, `font`                                                               |
|`{category}`         |`logo`, `mark`, `icon`, `banner`, `bg`, `pfp`, `cover`, `color`                             |
|`{variant}`          |`full`, `rounded`, `tagline`, `grid`, `gradient`, `youtube`, `facebook`, `whatsapp`, `gmail`|
|`{theme}`            |`electric-aqua`, `midnight-teal`, `soft-white`, `electric-blue`, `gradient`                 |
|`{size}` *(optional)*|`2560x1440`, `820x312`, `300px`                                                             |
|`{v}` *(optional)*   |`v1`, `v2`, `v3` — when multiple versions of the same asset exist                           |

**Rules:**

1. All lowercase, no spaces, no underscores — hyphens only
1. Brand prefix is always first (`aioverse-` / `aiotize-`); fonts use `font-`
1. No parentheses, dots, or special characters in filenames
1. SVG and WebP of the same asset share the same base name
1. Duplicate assets are versioned with `-v{N}` suffix before extension
1. All docs live in `docs/` with readable kebab names

See [`docs/NAMING_CONVENTION.md`](docs/NAMING_CONVENTION.md) for the full spec and rename mapping.

